credentials.json
**/credentials.json
# Exception: a public CA certificate, not a credential. It is the Supabase
# pooler's self-signed root, which no public trust store contains, so scripts
# that open a database connection need it in the repository to verify the
# server instead of falling back to rejectUnauthorized:false. It contains no
# private key — `openssl x509` on it prints a certificate, and the matching key
# lives only at Supabase. server/db.ts carries the same bytes inline and
# server/db.test.ts asserts the two match.
!certs/supabase-root-2021.pem
*.key
supabase/key.txt

